apple:movie-start","objectID":"4DD712C4-3784-45DD-9D05-855A31FF3B66"}],"automaticPlay":true,"hyperlinks":[],"accessibility":[{"text":"set<Fraction> does not compile. ","targetRectangle":{"y":229.72444152832031,"x":111.69918060302734,"width":622.37424218750004,"height":65.063995361328125}},{"text":"A set keeps its elements sorted, so it has to ask \\\"is this one less than that one?\\\", and Fraction has no answer.","targetRectangle":{"y":294.78843688964844,"x":111.69918060302734,"width":963.76713281249977,"height":101.06399536132812}},{"text":"Tell the class what < means by writing operator<. It is a member function with an unusual name, like operator= last week.","targetRectangle":{"y":470.84280395507812,"x":108.51803588867188,"width":950.35795257812515,"height":145.71129675388329}},{"text":"Without operator< the error is no match for 'operator<', and it points into a library header, not at your code. Read down the message to find your line.","targetRectangle":{"y":616.55410070896141,"x":141.27803838271848,"width":932.09552515625046,"height":140.70823614597327}},{"text":"a < b on two Fractions is the call a.operator<(b).","targetRectangle":{"y":757.26233685493469,"x":141.27803838271848,"width":880.12097468750028,"height":58.708236145973274}},{"text":"The same operator< lets sort work on a vector<Fraction> and lets Fraction be the key of a map.","targetRectangle":{"y":815.97057300090796,"x":141.27803838271848,"width":887.50758687500047,"height":150.64470770359037}},{"text":"It must be const: the container only has read access to its elements.","targetRectangle":{"y":966.61528070449833,"x":141.27803838271848,"width":920.46732476562511,"height":85.999999999999886}},{"text":"Your own class as a key","targetRectangle":{"y":79,"x":99,"width":930.6650008359552,"height":100.53440856933594}}],"baseLayer":{"animations":[],"initialState":{"affineTransform":[1,0,0,1,0,0],"masksToBounds":false,"rotation":0,"scale":1,"position":{"pointX":960,"pointY":540},"width":1920,"sublayerT